# Cursor Context Compress MCP

When the **cursor-context-compress-mcp** plugin is enabled, prefer these MCP tools over raw Shell/Read/Grep for the same tasks.

## Tool routing

| Task | Tool |
|------|------|
| `git status`, `git diff`, `git log`, commits | `rtk_git` |
| Read file with RTK filtering | `rtk_read` |
| List / grep / find | `rtk_ls`, `rtk_grep`, `rtk_find` |
| Shell command output | `rtk_shell` |
| Compress arbitrary text / JSON | `claw_compress_text` |
| Compress chat / message history | `claw_compress_messages` |
| Restore Claw-compressed section | `claw_rewind` |
| RTK-only savings report | `rtk_gain` |
| **Both engines - savings dashboard** | `compress_stats` |
| Token estimate only | `rtk_count_tokens` |
| Workspace compression estimate | `claw_workspace_benchmark` |

## Token savings

When the user asks about **token savings**, **gain**, **stats**, or **how much we saved**:

- Call `compress_stats` with `engines: all` and `scope: project` when working in a project workspace.
- Or use command `/cursor-context-compress-mcp-stats`.

Do not duplicate RTK hooks and MCP for the same shell command.

## Setup

If tools fail with "not found", run `/cursor-context-compress-mcp-doctor` or skill `cursor-context-compress-mcp-setup` - do not install RTK/Claw without user consent.
